 79_2421 .sqs-html-content { } } @media screen and (max-width: 767px) { } T
 here’s nothing as entertaining as hearing folks from the past explain ho
 w things used to be—here guests learn about the oldest profession as it 
 was practiced in Petaluma during the early 20th century\, from the madame 
 herself! Hear stories from people who worked the egg trade\, ran messages 
 between businesses\, managed boarding houses\, and built enterprises that 
 fueled a growing city. As you move through downtown and along historic riv
 erbanks\, you’ll gain a deeper appreciation for the ingenuity\, industri
 ous spirit\, and daily lives that shaped Petaluma—and the river that mad
 e it all possible. No paddling experience necessary. All equipment and ins
 truction provided. Just bring your curiosity—and be ready to see Petalum
 a through new eyes. #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1778182927579_4668 { --stroke-styl
